e">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Bir Singh Deo, also called Virasimha, was a Tomara Rajput chief who founded the Tomara dynasty of Gwalior in the late 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/birchtown"><span class="enc-name">Birchtown</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Birchtown is a community near Shelburne in Nova Scotia, Canada, founded in 1783 by about 1,500 Black Loyalists who had escaped slavery to support the British in the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/birendra-of-nepal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/birendra-of-nepal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Birendra of Nepal</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Birendra (1945–2001) was king of Nepal from 1972 to 2001.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/birger-jarl"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/birger-jarl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Birger Jarl</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Birger Jarl was a Swedish statesman who held the office of jarl from 1248 and governed for his son King Valdemar, founding the Folkung dynasty.</span></a></li></ul>
